# LJ minimization SCALING deck matching the Atomiverse CPU minimizer
# benchmark (benchmarks/md/lj/performance/minimize_scaling.cpp). Distinct
# from in.lj_min_kk (single-GPU CONVERGENCE benchmark, fcc rho*=1.0, reads a
# data file): this deck measures fixed-work throughput at 1..N MPI ranks.
# Reduced LJ units:
#   sigma = epsilon = 1, simple-cubic rho* = 0.712, cutoff = 2 sigma,
#   skin = 0.6 sigma, ~0.04-lattice-unit random displacement (= AV's 0.1-A
#   jitter at spacing 2.8 A) as the perturbation the minimizer relaxes.
# LAMMPS-benchmark convention: etol = ftol = 0 so the iteration budget is
# always exhausted — fixed work at every rank count. NB the sc rho*=0.712
# lattice is mechanically unstable under FULL relaxation (it would collapse
# toward fcc — see in.lj_min_kk); within the fixed 100-iteration budget the
# displacements stay < 0.03 lattice units and the per-iteration work is
# uniform, which is all a throughput benchmark needs. Run:
#   mpirun -n <P> lmp -in in.lj_min_scale_kk -v cells <L> -v iters <N>
# Atom count = cells^3.
#
# Work-unit note: LAMMPS min_style cg does a line search (typically ~2 force
# evaluations per iteration); the AV optimizers are fixed-alpha (exactly 1
# feval per iteration). Compare via Matom-FEVAL/s using the "Force
# evaluations" count printed in the minimize stats block, not iterations.
variable        cells index 64
variable        iters index 100
variable        evals equal 100*${iters}

units           lj
atom_style      atomic
lattice         sc 0.712
region          box block 0 ${cells} 0 ${cells} 0 ${cells}
create_box      1 box
create_atoms    1 box
mass            1 1.0
displace_atoms  all random 0.04 0.04 0.04 12345 units lattice

pair_style      lj/cut 2.0
pair_coeff      1 1 1.0 1.0

neighbor        0.6 bin
neigh_modify    every 1 delay 0 check yes

min_style       cg
minimize        0 0 ${iters} ${evals}
# Throughput is parsed from LAMMPS's standard
# "Loop time of <t> on <P> procs for <steps> steps with <atoms> atoms" line
# plus the "Force evaluations" count in the minimize stats block.
